// REQUIRES: clang
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-cabi-sigs.py %gopp 1 40 amd64 %t.amd64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-cabi-sigs.py %gopp 0 300 amd64 %t.ea --edges
// SPLIT: cabi-signatures 1/2
// P04.11 (D4.4): the IR signature of a C function as Go++ declares it (the
// parameter and result types, signext/zeroext, byval and sret with their
// types and alignment, alignstack, dead_on_return) is the one Clang gives
// the same C function, for generated signatures (Inputs/check-cabi-sigs.py;
// tests/run/Inputs/gen-cabi.py makes them). It needs no run, so it also holds
// on a machine that cannot run arm64. The same for 300 of the enumerated edge
// signatures (gen-cabi.py --mode edges) per target. Many more, and every
// edge: cabi-signatures.long.test.
